    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49-a8">

                <pb facs="0124" n="56" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg56"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 8—Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitlock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your letter September twenty third<anchor n="9" xml:id="d49-f1"/> and my replies
                    October 9th and eleventh. Miss Cavell sentenced yesterday and executed at two
                    o’clock this morning despite our best efforts continued until the last
                        moment.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d49-f2"/> Full report follows by mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitlock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d49-f1" n="9" xml:id="d49-f1-content">
                <p>No copy enclosed with this despatch.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d49-f2" n="10" xml:id="d49-f2-content">
                <p>Minister Whitlock states in his book <hi rendition="#italic">Belgium Under the
                        German Occupation</hi> (London, 1919), vol. II, p. 24, “I was mistaken in
                    supposing that the execution had taken place at two o’clock.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
